{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_course_modal

    The course dialogue's frame: core/modal itself, with three blocks of it changed. The dialogue
    carries the plugin's own class, which every rule of its stylesheet is qualified by, and the
    header keeps core's close button and a visually hidden title - the course's visible title lives
    on the cover inside the body, so that it scrolls away with the picture it is printed on, and
    the header is laid over the cover's corner. The hidden title is what core's root is labelled
    by until categorycoursemodal hands that id to the cover's title and removes it, so the dialogue
    has one heading, the one a reader sees; the body and the footer stay core's blocks, which the
    module fills with the two parts of the card's own category_card_modal.
    The hidden title keeps core's data-region="title": core/modal's constructor raises an exception
    when the header has none.

    Everything core/modal brings is kept: the focus trap, Escape, the close button, the backdrop
    and the focus given back to the control that opened it.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Atendimento Pré-Hospitalar",
        "body": "<div class=\"dim-cmodal__sheet\"><h2 class=\"dim-cmodal__title\" data-region=\"title\">Atendimento Pré-Hospitalar</h2></div>",
        "footer": "<div class=\"dim-cmodal__actions\"><a class=\"btn dim-cmodal__button dim-cmodal__button--primary\" href=\"https://example.com/course/view.php?id=42\">Continuar curso</a></div>"
    }
}}
{{< core/modal }}
    {{$classes}}dim-cmodal__dialog{{/classes}}
    {{$headerclasses}}dim-cmodal__close{{/headerclasses}}
    {{$header}}
        <h2 id="{{uniqid}}-modal-title" class="visually-hidden" data-region="title">{{title}}</h2>
    {{/header}}
{{/ core/modal }}
